.Dd September 16, 2026
.Dt NDI_RA_REQUEST 9S
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ndi_ra_request ,
.Nm ndi_ra_request_t
.Nd bus resource allocation request
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/sunndi.h
.Sh INTERFACE LEVEL
illumos specific
.Pq Consolidation Private .
.Sh DESCRIPTION
An \fBndi_ra_request_t\fP supplies constraints to \fBndi_ra_alloc()\fP.
Zero-initialize the structure before setting the required members.
Use the resource's units for all addresses and lengths: memory and I/O maps
normally use bytes, while bus-number and interrupt maps use resource numbers.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Va ra_flags
Bitwise OR of the request flags described below.
.It Va ra_len
Requested length.
Supply a nonzero value.
.It Va ra_addr
Requested base address when \fBNDI_RA_ALLOC_SPECIFIED\fP is set.
.It Va ra_boundbase , ra_boundlen
Base and length of the allocation window when
\fBNDI_RA_ALLOC_BOUNDED\fP is set.
Use a nonempty window and avoid overflowing the address space.
.It Va ra_align_mask
Alignment mask for an automatically selected base.
For power-of-two alignment A, use A - 1; zero requests no additional alignment.
This member is ignored with \fBNDI_RA_ALIGN_SIZE\fP.
.El
.Pp
The request flags are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Dv NDI_RA_ALIGN_SIZE
Use \fBra_len - 1\fP as the alignment mask.
\fBra_len\fP must be a nonzero power of two.
.It Dv NDI_RA_ALLOC_BOUNDED
Restrict automatic selection to the specified allocation window.
.It Dv NDI_RA_ALLOC_SPECIFIED
Request the base in \fBra_addr\fP.
The fixed-address path does not apply the automatic alignment adjustment.
Callers must ensure the specified address and requested range meet their
alignment and window requirements.
.It Dv NDI_RA_ALLOC_PARTIAL_OK
Permit a smaller range when the complete request cannot be met.
A partial allocation returns \fBNDI_RA_PARTIAL_REQ\fP and consumes the returned
range; inspect the returned length before using it.
.El
.Pp
\fBNDI_RA_PASS\fP is a separate map-lookup flag passed to the allocator function,
not a member of \fBra_flags\fP.
The request structure remains owned by the caller.
Allocation results are returned through the function's output arguments,
not by updating this structure.
.Sh STRUCTURE MEMBERS
.Bd -literal -offset indent
uint_t          ra_flags;
uint64_t        ra_len;
uint64_t        ra_addr;
uint64_t        ra_boundbase;
uint64_t        ra_boundlen;
uint64_t        ra_align_mask;
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ndi_ra_alloc 9F ,
.Xr sunndi 9F
